# docs.gerillass.com -> gerillass.com/docs
#
# The documentation moved from its own subdomain into a folder of the site.
# Every page kept its slug, so this is one line per page rather than a rule:
# a pattern would have had to guess, and a redirect that guesses wrong is a
# soft 404 in the eyes of a crawler.
#
# Both the trailing-slash and bare forms are listed. Hugo served the first and
# the new site serves the second, so a link written either way lands in one
# hop instead of two.
#
# Generated by diffing the old sitemap against the new one: 80 URLs
# there, 76 of them pages that exist at the new address.
#
# Keep these for at least 180 days, and longer while Search Console still
# reports traffic to the old property. Google needs to recrawl each URL to see
# its redirect, so leave the old sitemap in place while that happens.

# The old documentation home was Getting Started, which is now Introduction.
/                    https://gerillass.com/docs/introduction    301!

# Hugo's taxonomy pages. They listed the documentation rather than being part
# of it, so they go where a reader looking for the documentation should land.
/docs/               https://gerillass.com/docs/introduction    301!
